A||||21||007DOUG||What's 88 Fiero #6 worth? Neat story.||||5||
Z||000000||007DOUG||03-04-2000||04:17 PM||||Here in my home town, my high school (of many years ago) has an 88 GT in the automotive shop class. GM donated the car to the school. Every other year, GM donates a car. Another noteworthy car is a  T-type Le Sabre.  Most are Lemons that just can't be re-sold. But not the fiero.<P>The car has 6K, is a 5 speed, hardtop, grey cloth with all power, wing, and black wheels. Its the "one of 241 yellow". <P>Oh yeah, Its VIN is 200006<P>If I understand correct,  yellow wasn't available till mid-year. Also, on the front of the GTis a  "MOTOR TREND" license plate. Was this a "press car"? I've never gone and looked at back issuses of of MT.<P>Now the sad part, The car can never be sold, licensed, titled, driven......etc. It must be scrapped.<P>At least the automotive shop teacher knows what he's got. (he did mention how hard it was in the past to send chevelles onto the scrapper). He says he'll try to keep it here forever, and that makes him, my new best friend. <P>So, whats it worth? Not that we can buy it.<P>Does it belong in a school, or my garage? I keep thinking about "borrowing" the car for a millenium or two.<P>Should it be insured by State Farm, or Loyd's of London?<P>I'll try to get pics of the car and post them on my site, sometime this summer when schools out.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||03-04-2000||04:56 PM||||Could they donate it to anyone?  If they're through with it, you could get a nice conversation piece.||||reg||1
Z||000002||sid1200||03-04-2000||05:42 PM||||This indeed sounds like the Motor Trend, I have an issue, April 88 I belive and it features a yellow GT like the one you're describing.  Hope it doesn't go to the scrapper. Maybe the school could "lose" it or something.  And maybe I could "find" it or another list member.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
