Z||000006||batboy||03-04-2000||08:59 PM||||You could get an old beater 88 Fiero with a title, strip it down to the space frame and then transfer all the yellow 88 parts over to it. A lot of work, but a restored car.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||03-04-2000||09:56 PM||||That stinks- My vocational school got an 88 Citation with 6 miles on it and you got the Fiero! Good news, I have heard of being able to title these donated cars. Because of the donation thing and having to have the car dismantled and sold as scrap pose problems to most people, but it can be done. The instructor can "dismantle" the car. You can buy it at scrap price and reassemble the car, apply for an "abandoned vehicle title" or see what one of the car rebuilders in your area recommend and see what happens. Better yet- Apply for the title first. That way if it doesnt go through, you will not get your hopes too high. The best news here is that it can be done! Good Luck.<p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 03-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||03-05-2000||06:47 AM||||Just have them sent it to Rhode Island (my house is best). As I've said before we don't need a title if the car is over 10 yrs old only a VIN and a bill of sale is required for registration. Then to sell out of state you just apply to your own state for a new title.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula||03-05-2000||08:47 AM||||This might sound illegal but couldnt you find a beat up 88 GT and swap the vin numbers?  (change the dash and forget about the vin on accident, but remember it later and go back to get 200006 and hang it on your wall)<P>You didnt hear this for me..........||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phil||03-05-2000||08:50 AM||||I believe on the 88's all the body panels have the VIN on them also. In addition the VIN is in several locations  on the body to pervent that sort of swap.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cooter||03-05-2000||10:39 AM||||Yes Formula, that would be illegal. If the vehicle cannot be titled, buy it as scrap and find a 88 base coupe to transfer all the body panels and driveline into. The good thing about this-you can have it insured as a base coupe and save a ton of money!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Monkeyman||03-05-2000||02:44 PM||||Although, if you insure it as a base coupe, make darn sure you submit plenty of pics to your insurance agent.  Otherwise, when you file a claim and they total the car, they'll only pay you book value for a 12 year old coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Phil||03-05-2000||03:09 PM||||Monkey <BR>That usually doesn't work, they say if your car is much above market you should have an agreed value policy. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cooter||03-05-2000||03:25 PM||||Phil, you beat me to it. It doesnt matter to your insurance company if the 12 year old car is a base coupe, gt, formula or anything. They are not going to pay what the car is worth, especially if you have something super nice. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Monkeyman||03-05-2000||08:37 PM||||Progressive told me that, if I made any modifications to my car that would increase the value, I should send them pics so that they could adjust the amount my car is worth.  You guys must have a different insurance company.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Phil||03-05-2000||09:02 PM||||Bet ya if they increase the value of your car the premium will increase proportionaly||||reg||1
Z||000017||007DOUG||03-05-2000||11:09 PM||||sid 1200.......thanx for the info. Amazing that such a special car found its way to my  hometown.<P>Someday this car's time will be up. And believe me, a thousand ideas have run through my head about how to get this car. We'll see what happens. ||||reg||12
Z||000018||Monkeyman||03-06-2000||05:57 AM||||Phil--Undoubtably your rates would increase.  I was just stating that, if you insure a car as a base model and total it, you'll only get what the insurance co feels that a base model is worth.  If what you really have is a base model (VIN) and a GT body/interior/susp/motor/etc, you should let your insurance agent know so, in the event that something does happen to it, you can get more $$.  Most of the time you'll need to show proof (pics) of the changes in the car and possibly some reciepts.  This is what I'll have to do with the '85 GT as it has custom paint and aftermarket wheels.  It won't make much difference in the premiums (something like $27/yr), but it will allow me to get the car repainted the same color(s) if something happens to it.||||reg||1
