Z||000020||william_thorniii||03-06-2000||05:55 PM||||Doug,<P>You really need to consult the shop teacher on this one.  I have heard of another case in which a test mule that a teacher dismantled with a water jet cutter.  Fortunately for the car, he only damaged the body.  This car was purchased from the scrap yard.  <P>Ed Parks of the Fiero Factory (in Toney, AL) can get you a title.  He does this all the time.  Give him a call, he should be able to help you out.  <P>If something happens and you can't follow through with this let me know.  I would love to see that a wonderful Fiero get into some deserving hands.. and WV isn't too far away and well worth the trip.<P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>937-259-5295||||reg||10
Z||000021||007DOUG||03-06-2000||09:39 PM||||The teacher has assured me he'll keep the car as long as possible. I gave him the 88 build #'s and showed him how few yellow GT's were made. When the times up, he'll let me know.<P>I figure I'll be 2nd in line for the car anyways. The teacher himself owns an 88 Gt with t-tops (I have never seen the car, but he told me he rescued it from a local salvage yard in poor shape). I'm sure he'll get what he wants from it, or swap VINs.<P>If anyone is ever in the area, I'll show you where it is. Even when school is closed, you can see it through the windows (OK, maybe not the same as ACTUALLY touching or sitting in it).<P>William......Thanx. Come visit me anytime. I've talked to Ed many times. An excellent man and great work (just visit "my garage" on my webpage). I'm sure that something can be arranged when the time comes. If it comes. <P>This car belongs somewhere other than where it is. ||||reg||14
